{"id": "EUVD-2026-93102", "enisaUuid": "d6ff0ce1-5710-3311-bcab-59ba0c919d14", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix rlist race and missing initialization\n\nTCP_Server_Info.rlist is allocated via kzalloc which zeros both ->next\nand ->prev to NULL instead of pointing to itself, making list_empty()\nalways return false and list_add() dereference a NULL ->prev pointer.\n\nAlso, cifs_signal_cifsd_for_reconnect() can be called concurrently\nfrom multiple cifsd threads, allowing the same server's rlist node to\nbe added twice into the local list, corrupting it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:05", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5f924ffbfa976e4b97f17e8132c595b97482c2d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a8f82f9c5839389cf4036029dd75a9911049e83", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04082b1833856cb9ed87e0d3d5f04cbf836cf7da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c037d6bde3dd5fa00b017b6b98a5389ec0ebc02f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f270f091256da1338c3631083e15d7f83cc05e1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f559-3m6w-qcp7", "CVE-2026-98174"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b6960da-949e-33ad-8166-72134f3a374a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "33a64aa6-60fd-3f5c-bcb9-969306a02860", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "345aafaf-2e97-36bf-bf7f-48d7a4e64b3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "4a9e6b19-c896-3d89-9452-4a1fd5fd6775", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "5400765b-e92b-3d49-ba77-acfc90b4886d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux